<title>UK: Lex to sell 11 mln Synnex shares.</title>
<headline>Lex to sell 11 mln Synnex shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British vehicle leasing company Lex Service Plc said on Monday it was selling 11 million of its current holding of 36.8 million shares, in Taiwan's Synnex Technology International Corp.  </p>
<p>Lex will retain 25.8 million shares, or 17.2 percent, in the Taiwanese electronics distributor.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it would provide further details during publication of first-half results on July 25.</p>
<p>Shares in Lex pushed higher following the announcement, gaining 14p to 389p by 1622 GMT.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
